      "transcript_text": "Now let us talk about private and public corporations from the Indian standpoint. What are the key differences between a private limited company and a public limited company? Let us talk about minimum number of shareholders. A private limited company needs to have a minimum of two shareholders, while a public limited company needs to have a minimum of seven shareholders. As far as the maximum number of shareholders are concerned, a private limited company can have no more than 200 shareholders. While there is no restriction on the number of shareholders that a public limited company can have. Also, let us talk about minimum paid up capital, which is needed to start a private limited company and a public limited company. Believe it or not, regulations do not require any minimum paid up capital. To start a private limited company, which means that you can start a private limited company with virtually no capital. On the other hand, if we talk about a public limited company, it requires a minimum of five lakh rupees of paid up capital. Now we have talked about some differences between private limited company and public limited company. However, I have not told to you as to what is the key difference which differentiates a private limited company from a public limited company. That difference lies in transferability of shares. In the case of a private limited company, the share transferability is restricted, which means that if you are a shareholder of a private limited company, you cannot easily transfer your shares or sell off your shares to somebody else. On the other hand, if you are a shareholder of a public limited company, you can easily sell off your shares to somebody else. So, your shares are freely transferable. That is the key difference between a private limited company and a public limited company. You might have a question. How do we know by looking at a name of a company as to whether a company is a private limited company or it is a public limited company? To identify a company as a private limited company, you have to look at its suffix. If the name of the company is ending with PBT, LTD, it tells you that the company is a private limited company. On the other hand, if the name of the company is simply ending with limited with no public included in it or private included in it, it will be called as a public limited company. For example, if we talk about Tata San's private limited, it is essentially a private limited company. On the other hand, if we talk about Tata still limited. Tata still limited since it is ending with only limited, it is a public limited company. Okay, I have a question for you. My question is whether it is a private limited company or it is a public limited company? Both the names have limited. Why? What is the meaning of the word limited? Why do we have limited at the end of the name of a company? What do you think? The reason is simple. The answer is simple. Both companies have their names ending in limited because it indicates that the liability of the owners of a company is limited. Okay, now you might have yet another question. Do all public limited companies have to be listed on a stock exchange? Can public limited companies also be unlimited companies? The answer is that a public limited company need not be a listed company. A public limited company can also be an unlisted company. Let me give you an example. If you talk about BSE limited, you must have heard about this name BSE. BSE stands for Bombay Stock Exchange. BSE limited is a listed company. The shares of BSE are listed on NSE. NSE stands for National Stock Exchange of India. Okay, now let us talk about NSE. NSE India limited. As you can figure out, it is also a public limited company because the name is ending with the word limited. However, as we speak, the shares of NSE India limited are not being traded on a stock exchange. In other words, NSE India limited is an unlisted company as we speak. However, NSE India limited is very soon planning to come up with something called as an IPO through which NSE India will become a listed company. You must be wondering, can a stock exchange listed shares on itself? In India, the regulations do not permit a stock exchange to listed shares on itself. In other words, for BSE to become a listed company, it had to get its shares listed on the NSE. And now NSE is also going to become very soon a listed firm by getting its shares listed on the BSE. Thank you.",
