      "transcript_text": "Let us now move on to another topic. Let us now talk about Corporate Investment and Financing Decisions, which means, investment and financing decisions undertaken by corporations. Almost all of you would have come across this country. This term called as investment. What is an investment? An investment means spending money today in the hope of making more money in the future or at least getting some benefit in the future. Wondering what is the difference between a real asset and a financial asset? What is a real asset? A real asset is a an asset that is used to produce goods and services. For example, if we talk about property, plant or equipment, these are all real assets. These assets are used to produce goods and services. You must be wondering whether real assets need to be tangible? Can real assets be intangible? The answer is yes, real assets of course can be intangible. Can you think of an intangible real asset? For example, if you talk about a patent, a patent is an intangible real asset. Now, let us talk about financial assets. What is a financial asset? A financial asset is for example, if we talk about a share, a bond, these are examples of financial assets. How do we define a financial asset? Financial asset is essentially a financial claim on the cash flows which are generated by your real assets. You understand that your company's real assets are going to be made use of to produce goods and services. These goods and services are going to generate cash flows and your financial assets are essentially claims on these cash flows. Now, let me ask you a few questions. You have to identify whether the following are tangible real assets, intangible real assets or financial assets. The first one, unsold goods on your store shelves. What is it? It is a tangible real asset. Next one, your company's reputation for customer service. What is it? It is an intangible real asset. As you might agree, this is a real asset. However, you cannot touch it and feel it. So, therefore, it is an intangible real asset. Next one, the negotiation scales of your company's sales force. What is it? Again, it is an intangible real asset. Okay, the last one. A 5% stake in your main supplier. When I say 5% stake, it means that you are holding 5% of the shares of your supplier. What kind of an asset is this? This is as you can figure out a financial asset.",
