      "transcript_text": "Let us move on to our next topic, which is financial goal of the corporation. You understand that firms often have hundreds of thousands of shareholders. If you talk about large firms like Infosys, they have millions of shareholders. For example, Infosys had more than 2 million shareholders holding more than 4 billion shares as of March 31st, 2026. Now the question before you is, can all these shareholders who are owners of a firm be actively involved in running the firm? The answer is no. Why? Because if these millions of shareholders are actively involved in running the firm, it will lead to all chaos. So therefore, what do you think shareholders need to do? Given that shareholders cannot manage the firm actively on their own, what do you think they need to do? They essentially need to delete the firm. They get their authority to somebody else. And what is that somebody else called as? That somebody else is professional managers. Okay, now another follow-up question for you is, we know that these shareholders, they differ in their ages, they differ in their tastes and preferences, they differ in their time horizons, they differ in the degree of their risk tolerance, they differ in their investment strategy and so on and so forth. So the question then is, how can a firm's managers make decisions that satisfy all shareholders? Put differently, will the delegation of authority from shareholders to managers work if yes, under what condition? Think about it. Under what condition will this arrangement of delegation of authority from shareholders to managers work? This arrangement of delegation of authority will work as long as shareholders have a common objective. Okay, you can anticipate my next question. My next question obviously is, therefore, what should be the common objective of shareholders? What do you think? What do shareholders want? Shareholders after all are human beings and human beings in general are greedy and therefore, they would prefer more wealth over less wealth at any given point in time. So therefore, what do you think should be the common objective of all shareholders? The common objective of all shareholders, therefore, should be to maximize their wealth, which means what? Which means maximizing the current stock price of the firm because shareholders are holding the shares and their wealth will be maximized if the current stock price is maximized. Now the question is, how can managers maximize the wealth of shareholders? Managers can maximize the wealth of shareholders by accepting value adding investment projects? You must be wondering, how do we know whether a project is value adding or value destroying? Okay, you will get to know this very soon.",
